BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-20_sun_half-marathon@trainingplan.local
DTSTAMP:20260818T033619Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:[Race] Half Marathon · 21km
DESCRIPTION:Session: 2026-09-20_sun_half-marathon\nType: race  ·  Status: 
 planned\n\nTargets:\n  - duration_min: 112\n  - distance_km: 21.1\n  - avg
 _hr_range: [139\, 147]\n  - avg_pace_min_per_km: 5:18\n  - pace_range_min_
 per_km: ['5:15'\, '5:22']\n\nNotes:\n*** RACE *** Half marathon — 21.1 k
 m.\n\nA-goal 1:52 (5:18/km). B-goal 1:56 (5:30/km). Stretch: PR pace 5:12 
 (1:49:42) only if the Sep 1 checkpoint was green.\n\nThis target is set of
 f what the last four months actually contained\, not off ambition: best 5 
 km split 26:00\, two runs over 10 km since April\, a back injury in late J
 uly. 1:52 off that base is a real six-week gain.\n\nPacing\n  Km 1-3: 5:18
 \, never faster. This is the failure mode — going out at a pace the trai
 ning didn't buy turns 1:52 into 2:05.\n  Km 4-15: lock in 5:15-5:22\, HR 1
 39-147. Rhythm over heroics.\n  Km 16-21: race. Empty it in the last 3 km\
 , not at 16.\n\nDecision gate (set after the Sep 1 checkpoint)\n  Green 
 — 3x2 km at 5:15 felt controlled → race at 5:18\, and if it felt genui
 nely easy consider 5:12 for a PR.\n  Amber — it was a fight → race at 
 5:30 and negative-split.\n\nFueling\n  Breakfast 2.5-3 h out\, familiar ca
 rbs.\n  1 gel ~15 min before start\, 1 gel around km 10-12.\n  Water at st
 ations — a few sips each\, don't skip.\n\nIf the day goes sideways\n  HR
  over 150 in the first 5 km → ease off 10 s/km immediately.\n  Back tigh
 tens → shorten stride\, lift cadence\, don't fight it. A finished 2:00 b
 eats a walked 18 km.
DTSTART:20260920T060000
DTEND:20260920T075200
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
